From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:16:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/46] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-xiaomi-diting: Fix PM8350C L3
 and PM8450 L4

Found on the first boot of the device (console photo, 2026-10-11):
- vreg_l3c_3p3: 3.300 V is not a valid step of this PMIC5 PLDO
  (1.504 V + n * 8 mV), so the whole PM8350C regulator device failed to
  probe, which left the UFS and eUSB2 PHYs without L10C.
- PM8450 ldo4: 'could not find RPMh address for resource ldoh4'; the
  regulator is not in this unit's command DB.

Local Diting bring-up patch, not submitted upstream.
---
 .../arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts | 16 +++++++---------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
index 4809aab0f..e77871ab1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
@@ -240,11 +240,14 @@ vreg_l2c_1p8: ldo2 {
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
 
-		/* always-on and boot-on in the vendor DT */
+		/*
+		 * always-on and boot-on in the vendor DT, which asks for 3.3 V;
+		 * this PLDO only has 3.296/3.304 V steps around it.
+		 */
 		vreg_l3c_3p3: ldo3 {
 			regulator-name = "vreg_l3c_3p3";
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <3300000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <3296000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <3304000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 			regulator-boot-on;
 			regulator-always-on;
@@ -345,12 +348,7 @@ vreg_l3h_0p87: ldo3 {
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
 
-		vreg_l4h_1p8: ldo4 {
-			regulator-name = "vreg_l4h_1p8";
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <1808000>;
-			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
-		};
+		/* ldo4: listed in the vendor DT, but absent from this unit's cmd-db */
 	};
 
 	regulators-3 {
